Mark write<double, true> with MFBT_API

First-party code uses Zmij through headers that other libraries include,
so the zmij::detail::write<double, true>() instantiation referenced by
zmij::write_ecmascript() must be resolvable anywhere those headers are
used. Links that pull in mozglue but not libxul or libjs resolve it from
the shared mozglue library, which does not export hidden-visibility
symbols, and the whole build is compiled with hidden visibility. Apply
MFBT_API in two places:

* on the explicit instantiation in zmij.cc, so the definition is
  exported from the shared mozglue library, and
* on an "extern template" declaration in zmij.h, so that consumer TUs
  compiled with hidden visibility emit default-visibility references.
Index: zmij/zmij.cc
===================================================================
--- zmij.orig/zmij.cc
+++ zmij/zmij.cc
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
